{"id": "EUVD-2026-81739", "enisaUuid": "2e152622-f74f-3afa-abea-f6d422d29e26", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf, xdp: move offload check into dev_xdp_install()\n\nbpf_xdp_link_update() calls dev_xdp_install() directly and skips\ndev_xdp_attach(), so the checks in dev_xdp_attach() do not run. A user can\nmake an XDP link with a normal program and then swap in an offloaded or\ndevice-bound program with BPF_LINK_UPDATE, which puts it on the software\npath.\n\ndev_xdp_install() is the one place all three paths go through:\n\"ip link set xdp\" and BPF_LINK_CREATE reach it via dev_xdp_attach(), and\nBPF_LINK_UPDATE calls it directly. So move the program checks (offloaded,\nbound to another device, device-bound in generic mode, native vs generic,\nDEVMAP and CPUMAP) there, and keep only the netlink-flag check\n(XDP_FLAGS_UPDATE_IF_NOEXIST) in dev_xdp_attach().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:04", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd06033625ec20b7bdec43d21f776fc1a5e9000e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/486dbe7efec2be19cd3625be282f7f6b34a3f2c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f14b774ec9bd52d0f4ec29a6597a35fd107197f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea7b35dcc9430293b861bc7bad0c546f193c85f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03022dd874070768a7099f18b1944c633641315f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad27ed7d2309419a129078d781504f486b1b469a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90146", "GHSA-7c8h-xm4v-9jxx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06463a4a-53d8-306a-931e-6d2fa924925a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026a4c28e1db3b0cb99cd9a3e495d4a8b632fa74 <bd06033625ec20b7bdec43d21f776fc1a5e9000e"}, {"id": "10684e5c-063e-3372-9778-d4ca092076d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "35d6d4e1-c138-3f84-a3d8-d9a7a7ffd87b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026a4c28e1db3b0cb99cd9a3e495d4a8b632fa74 <ea7b35dcc9430293b861bc7bad0c546f193c85f9"}, {"id": "64e8905c-716d-37b8-bbf3-6b5bbdded57c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "6eae5a27-b534-3863-a68b-778e4cea456f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026a4c28e1db3b0cb99cd9a3e495d4a8b632fa74 <486dbe7efec2be19cd3625be282f7f6b34a3f2c5"}, {"id": "8cd3854a-679d-32a0-8f4d-9560c01dfda0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "905d2f16-1ad9-38ae-98f5-058cc5981e79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "b13db5d0-4034-31a9-8f2d-1311852461be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "c98216ba-2cb2-3d83-aaa3-bb5665994a1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "cdef9daf-1eba-3e1b-a1e7-48800c4d7684", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026a4c28e1db3b0cb99cd9a3e495d4a8b632fa74 <03022dd874070768a7099f18b1944c633641315f"}, {"id": "d7af969b-9dda-32ce-b9d4-13f4bbe835a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026a4c28e1db3b0cb99cd9a3e495d4a8b632fa74 <f14b774ec9bd52d0f4ec29a6597a35fd107197f9"}, {"id": "ddfa64ac-bbbc-3053-861e-9714381ecfa5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026a4c28e1db3b0cb99cd9a3e495d4a8b632fa74 <ad27ed7d2309419a129078d781504f486b1b469a"}, {"id": "e3b786ec-37dc-37a1-88de-5c09e966ab6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.9"}, {"id": "fdf81440-d817-3083-b4d9-a23d29a78